# Copy to .env. The server reads it when it starts, and docker compose passes
# it on. WebDAV, TMDB and ffmpeg are set on the dashboard's Adapters page, not
# here.

# The first superuser, made on the first start. Take the password out of this
# file once it exists.
# FOYER_ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.com
# FOYER_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Behind a reverse proxy only: the header it puts the caller's address in. Never
# without a proxy — anyone could send it, and claim any address.
# FOYER_TRUST_PROXY=X-Forwarded-For

# The host port docker compose publishes: 8090, or 127.0.0.1:8090 behind a
# reverse proxy on the same machine.
# FOYER_PUBLISH=8090

# With compose.gpu.yaml: the host's render group, which may open
# /dev/dri/renderD128 — `getent group render | cut -d: -f3`.
# FOYER_RENDER_GID=

# Only where libva picks the wrong driver for the GPU: iHD for Intel from
# Broadwell on, i965 for older Intel, radeonsi for AMD.
# LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME=iHD
